    "result_text": "Tests are green. \n\nI agreed with the finding and fixed it. The change:\n\n- **Added `OwnerRegion.isKnownRegion(String)`** \u2014 a predicate backed by the same canonical `REGION_POSTCODES` map that already defines the region vocabulary, so there's one source of truth.\n- **`OwnerSegment`** now calls `OwnerRegion.isKnownRegion(locality)` instead of its own `Set.of(\"NSW\", \"VIC\", \"QLD\")`. The forked list is gone, so if a region is ever added to `OwnerRegion`'s tables the METRO/REGIONAL split tracks it automatically \u2014 restoring the \"can never drift\" guarantee.\n\nI used an explicit `isKnownRegion` predicate rather than the `!UNKNOWN.equals(locality)` sentinel trick: it reads as the actual concept (\"is this a known region\") and treats any unexpected value (including `null`) as REGIONAL via `Map.containsKey`, which also makes the null-locality branch a non-issue without relying on the caller always passing `UNKNOWN`. Full suite: BUILD SUCCESS, 2/2 acceptance tests passing.",
